Finding: {"title":"Standby-aircraft routes never verify :locationId belongs to the caller's org (cross-tenant write/read)","severity":"HIGH","area":"Security / Multi-Tenant Isolation","files":["src/server/routes/routes-standby-aircraft.ts"],"detail":"All 6 routes in this file (lines 274, 451, 492, 555, 608, 752) call `resolveOrgIdFromSession(authUser)` WITHOUT passing the Hono context `c`. This resolves `orgId` purely from the caller's own email/membership and never uses `:locationId` from the URL at all. Compare to the sibling file `routes-standby.ts`, which correctly calls `resolveOrgIdFromSession(authUser, c)` (with `c`) in every route — the `c` parameter is what lets `resolveOrgIdFromSession` (helpers.ts:325-339) derive/validate org from the location for super-admins, and more importantly there is NO other check anywhere in routes-standby-aircraft.ts that `locationId` belongs to `orgId`. A regular authenticated user from Org A can POST `/locations/{orgB-locationId}/schedule/standby-aircraft` and the row is written with their own `orgId` but an arbitrary `locationId` belonging to another school. Additionally, the activation conflict-check at line 628 calls `scheduleRepository.findByLocationAndDate(locationId, ...)`, which filters only by `locationId` with no `flightSchoolId` predicate (repository impl line 3780), so activation can read/report conflicts against another org's real schedule events.","impact":"A non-admin user can create, list, activate, or dismiss standby schedule events tied to another flight school's location — polluting another org's schedule and leaking scheduling data (student/instructor names, times) cross-tenant via the conflict-check response.","recommendation":"Pass `c` to `resolveOrgIdFromSession(authUser, c)` in every route in this file (matching routes-standby.ts), and additionally verify `locationId` resolves to the caller's `orgId` via `mvpRepository.locations.findFlightSchoolIdByLocation` (the same pattern used correctly in routes-aircraft-vor-log.ts's `ensureLocationAndAircraftAccess`). Also add `flightSchoolId`/orgId scoping to `findByLocationAndDate` in mvp-v2.repository.impl.ts.","confidence":"high"}
